            {
                "entry_id": "31af5e3f-b985-3b0d-a6d5-c937bcd18e9c",
                "word": "childs",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34409c26-c315-3e80-8178-d7463eedfc86",
                        "entry_id": "31af5e3f-b985-3b0d-a6d5-c937bcd18e9c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "plural of child"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "form-of",
                            "nonstandard",
                            "plural",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b42e2d4-3e9b-40dd-b4e8-f16885da1477",
                                "sense_id": "34409c26-c315-3e80-8178-d7463eedfc86",
                                "text": "You have been… searching! For… a child. No, no, no – two childs! A fine big boy… and a strange little boy. No, no, no… ahhh… a girl! A girl. A boy and a girl."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc3f9c23-a14b-4bfb-a743-156c5ceec469",
                                "sense_id": "34409c26-c315-3e80-8178-d7463eedfc86",
                                "text": "I remember one amusing episode: in a conversation with an engineer when responding to the usual Japanese enquiry in making social talk, \"How many childs have you?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d6db7e3-3d33-42db-923d-2402b3119a98",
                                "sense_id": "34409c26-c315-3e80-8178-d7463eedfc86",
                                "text": "\"It is as they say;\" he clucks; \"these childs are smoke the evil dope and the old ways of behave are forget."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8603ae25-3574-42fa-8b33-6d6ad074b226",
                                "sense_id": "34409c26-c315-3e80-8178-d7463eedfc86",
                                "text": "I can have many childs. Ten at a time at once."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5272e774-ee34-4e19-8b93-4f37dfa8c5b9",
                                "sense_id": "34409c26-c315-3e80-8178-d7463eedfc86",
                                "text": "Thus, the initial random vectors are all normalized and the childs are also normalized to unit vectors after any crossover or mutation operation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "220d6baa-da20-4ba7-a18a-13d1ad1855a8",
                                "sense_id": "34409c26-c315-3e80-8178-d7463eedfc86",
                                "text": "It is poison that has kill our little Rosemarie – and all her life ahead! The doctor say so – and he say I cannot understand about the rich man, why he do it. But I understand that the childs are dying."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "83b18f0a-925c-470b-9566-e489c0fe0d99",
                                "sense_id": "34409c26-c315-3e80-8178-d7463eedfc86",
                                "text": "We are not confused children and if we were then let these childs be free, for life is short and every bit of a smile extends life one more day."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
